msgctxt "page.title"
msgid "sus.bot | robots.txt checker"
msgstr "sus.bot | robots.txt-checker"

msgctxt "page.description"
msgid "Free robots.txt checker. Fetch any site's robots.txt, see which search engines and AI crawlers are allowed or blocked, test paths against the rules, and check how the server responds to different user-agents."
msgstr "Gratis robots.txt-checker. Haal de robots.txt van elke site op, zie welke zoekmachines en AI-crawlers zijn toegestaan of geblokkeerd, test paden tegen de regels en controleer hoe de server reageert op verschillende user-agents."

msgctxt "page.skip"
msgid "Skip to content"
msgstr "Naar de inhoud"

msgctxt "page.h1"
msgid "Check which crawlers your robots.txt lets in"
msgstr "Controleer welke crawlers je robots.txt binnenlaat"

msgctxt "page.themeLabel"
msgid "Colour theme"
msgstr "Kleurthema"

msgctxt "page.theme.system"
msgid "System"
msgstr "Systeem"

msgctxt "page.theme.light"
msgid "Light"
msgstr "Licht"

msgctxt "page.theme.dark"
msgid "Dark"
msgstr "Donker"

msgctxt "page.langLabel"
msgid "Language"
msgstr "Taal"

msgctxt "page.intro"
msgid "Enter a website. sus.bot fetches its <code>robots.txt</code> and shows which pages each search engine and AI crawler may visit. It also lists the paths the file reveals to anyone who reads it. The check runs in your browser and is free."
msgstr "Voer een website in. sus.bot haalt de <code>robots.txt</code> op en laat zien welke pagina's elke zoekmachine en elke AI-crawler mag bezoeken. Het toont ook de paden die het bestand prijsgeeft aan iedereen die het leest. De controle draait in je browser en is gratis."

msgctxt "page.urlLabel"
msgid "Website URL"
msgstr "Website-URL"

msgctxt "page.urlPlaceholder"
msgid "example.com"
msgstr "example.com"

msgctxt "page.analyse"
msgid "Analyse"
msgstr "Analyseren"

msgctxt "page.urlHint"
msgid "We fetch <code>/robots.txt</code> from the site's origin. Paths and query strings are ignored."
msgstr "We halen <code>/robots.txt</code> op vanaf de oorsprong van de site. Paden en querystrings worden genegeerd."

msgctxt "page.pasteSummary"
msgid "Paste a robots.txt instead"
msgstr "Of plak een robots.txt"

msgctxt "page.pasteLabel"
msgid "robots.txt contents"
msgstr "Inhoud van robots.txt"

msgctxt "page.analysePasted"
msgid "Analyse pasted text"
msgstr "Geplakte tekst analyseren"

msgctxt "page.loadExample"
msgid "Load the kitchen-sink example"
msgstr "Het alles-in-één-voorbeeld laden"

msgctxt "page.aiStatus"
msgid "AI scraping status"
msgstr "AI-scrapingstatus"

msgctxt "page.agents"
msgid "Crawler access"
msgstr "Toegang voor crawlers"

msgctxt "page.agentsIntro"
msgid "Resolved per crawler with RFC 9309 matching: the most specific group wins, then the longest rule, and ties go to <code>Allow</code>."
msgstr "Per crawler bepaald volgens RFC 9309: de meest specifieke groep wint, dan de langste regel, en bij gelijkspel <code>Allow</code>."

msgctxt "page.tester"
msgid "Test a path"
msgstr "Een pad testen"

msgctxt "page.access"
msgid "Real access by user-agent"
msgstr "Werkelijke toegang per user-agent"

msgctxt "page.accessIntro"
msgid "Request the file again through the proxy with each crawler's real user-agent string. A different status or body means the server treats that crawler differently (bot blocking, WAF rules, cloaking)."
msgstr "Vraag het bestand opnieuw op via de proxy met de echte user-agentstring van elke crawler. Een andere status of inhoud betekent dat de server die crawler anders behandelt (botblokkering, WAF-regels, cloaking)."

msgctxt "page.issues"
msgid "Issues"
msgstr "Problemen"

msgctxt "page.security"
msgid "Security notes"
msgstr "Beveiligingsnotities"

msgctxt "page.securityIntro"
msgid "Disallow rules that point at places attackers look for first. This checks what the file reveals, not whether the paths exist or are protected."
msgstr "Disallow-regels die wijzen naar plekken waar aanvallers als eerste kijken. Dit controleert wat het bestand prijsgeeft, niet of de paden bestaan of beveiligd zijn."

msgctxt "page.recon"
msgid "Reconnaissance"
msgstr "Verkenning"

msgctxt "page.reconIntro"
msgid "What a stranger learns about this site from the file alone: the platform it runs on, cloud buckets, other hostnames, API entry points, data feeds, file types, and notes left in comments. Nothing here is fetched or probed; it is read straight from the text."
msgstr "Wat een vreemde alleen uit het bestand over deze site leert: het platform, cloudbuckets, andere hostnamen, API-ingangen, datafeeds, bestandstypen en notities in opmerkingen. Niets hiervan wordt opgehaald of afgetast; alles wordt rechtstreeks uit de tekst gelezen."

msgctxt "page.sitemaps"
msgid "Sitemaps"
msgstr "Sitemaps"

msgctxt "page.raw"
msgid "File contents"
msgstr "Bestandsinhoud"

msgctxt "page.footerRfc"
msgid "Rule matching follows <a href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9309\" rel=\"noopener\">RFC 9309</a> and Google's published crawler behaviour."
msgstr "De regelmatching volgt <a href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9309\" rel=\"noopener\">RFC 9309</a> en het door Google gepubliceerde crawlergedrag."

msgctxt "page.footerBy"
msgid "A free tool by <a href=\"https://sitefig.eu\" rel=\"noopener\">Sitefig</a>."
msgstr "Een gratis tool van <a href=\"https://sitefig.eu\" rel=\"noopener\">Sitefig</a>."

msgctxt "page.noscript"
msgid "This tool runs entirely in your browser and needs JavaScript."
msgstr "Deze tool draait volledig in je browser en heeft JavaScript nodig."

